From 08b9e93dbc29231aeede99bb765959f107afd644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the opposite mate's length when computing mate 2's MAPQ

Since 41ee86b (MQ:i support) reportHits computed the MAPQ of mate 2
with mate 2's own length passed in the opposite-mate slot, so for a
concordant pair the perfect and minimum scores that BowtieMapq2 sums
over both mates were taken over mate 2 twice instead of mate 1 + mate 2.
With mates of unequal length the two mates of the same concordant pair
received different MAPQs: a 150/50-bp pair with 3 + 2 mismatches and no
second-best alignment gets 40 for mate 1 and 23 for mate 2; a 150/60-bp
pair in a two-copy repeat gets 6 and 30. Releases up to 2.5.4 gave both
mates the same value. Pass mate 1's length, as appendMate did before.
---
 aln_sink.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aln_sink.h b/aln_sink.h
index fe7db04..d0c0ffe 100644
--- a/aln_sink.h
+++ b/aln_sink.h
@@ -1373,7 +1373,7 @@ public:
                         staln2.buildMdz();
                         itoa10<TMapq>(mapq.mapq(summ, *flags2, rd2->mate < 2,
                                                 rd2->length(),
-                                                rd2 == NULL ? 0 : rd2->length(),
+                                                rd1 == NULL ? 0 : rd1->length(),
                                                 mapqInps2),
                                       buf2);
                         mapqs[1] = buf2;
